# Replaying a Batch is harmless; within one Batch the later timestamp wins for the same version.
@run = 1
@id = dup-{{run}}

### Same id and version twice, different payloads: both apply in timestamp order, 10:01 wins
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUsername}} {{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 1, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T10:01:00Z", "payload": { "title": "Second" } },
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 1, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T10:00:00Z", "payload": { "title": "First" } }
]

### Read it: title "Second"
GET {{host}}/entities/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic {{readerUsername}} {{readerPassword}}

### The same Batch again: both SkippedDuplicate
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUsername}} {{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 1, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T10:01:00Z", "payload": { "title": "Second" } },
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 1, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T10:00:00Z", "payload": { "title": "First" } }
]

### Read it: unchanged
GET {{host}}/entities/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic {{readerUsername}} {{readerPassword}}
